  "id": "ego-centered-network",
  "term": "ego-centered network",
  "definition": "An ego-centered network is a way of mapping a network from the viewpoint of one focal person or role. In the source, coordinators used ego-centered network maps to show how the surrounding network of connected actors was developing over time.",
